course: dictionary
lesson: 1601
title: The cheekbone
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Your cheekbones are the bones at the top of your cheeks, just below your eyes. You can find them by putting your fingers under your eyes and feeling for the hard bone.
explain: In a science lesson on the skeleton, you find the cheekbones on the skull, the bony frame that protects your brain. Your cheekbones are part of that frame.
explain: In stories, someone may have «high cheekbones». That describes the shape of a face, so a writer is painting a picture for you.
explain: Safety matters too: «A hard ball moves fast enough to break a nose, a tooth or a cheekbone, which is why helmets, face guards and mouth guards are worn.» Players wear protection because the face can be hurt.
fact: A cheekbone is one of the bones that make up the skull.
fact: «Cheekbone» is a noun. You have one cheekbone on each side, so two cheekbones in all.
fact: Your cheekbones sit at the top of your cheeks, just below your eyes.
fact: In a story, «high cheekbones» describes someone's face.
fact: A hard blow to the cheekbone can cause a bad bruise, so sports players wear face guards.
exercise: Where are your cheekbones? | *Just below your eyes, at the top of your cheeks | On your chin | Inside your ears | In your fingers
exercise: In a science lesson, where do pupils find the cheekbones? | *On the skull | In the hair | On the knee | In the heart
exercise: Why are helmets, face guards and mouth guards worn? | To make players look taller | *To protect the head and face from hard blows | To keep the face warm | To stop the ball from going fast
test: Someone in a story has «high cheekbones». What does this describe? | The sound of a voice | A kind of sports ball | *The shape of a person's face | A bone you can see through the skin
test: Which of these is a cheekbone? | A muscle in your arm | A bone in your toe | *A bone at the top of your cheek, just below your eye | A tooth at the back of your mouth
exam: What can a hard blow to the cheekbone cause? | A warm feeling | A new tooth | *A bad bruise | A longer nose
